# 2. Abstract

Polycystic Ovary Syndrome (PCOS) is one of the most common hormonal disorders affecting women. Early diagnosis is important because delayed detection may lead to infertility, metabolic disorders, and long-term health complications.

This project proposes a Convolutional Neural Network (CNN)-based deep learning system for automatic PCOS ultrasound image classification. The model was trained using a public ultrasound dataset containing infected and noninfected ovarian ultrasound images.

The workflow included data understanding, image preprocessing, data augmentation, imbalance handling using class weights, CNN model training, and comprehensive evaluation using accuracy, precision, recall, F1-score, ROC-AUC, confusion matrix, and threshold analysis.

Two CNN experiments were conducted to study overfitting and model generalization. The first CNN architecture achieved the best overall validation performance and was selected as the final model.

The final model achieved strong classification performance with high precision and good recall, demonstrating the effectiveness of CNNs for medical ultrasound image analysis.

