# 3. Introduction

## 3.1 Background

Polycystic Ovary Syndrome (PCOS) is a hormonal disorder that affects ovarian function in women. Ultrasound imaging is one of the primary diagnostic tools used by clinicians to identify ovarian abnormalities associated with PCOS.

Manual interpretation of ultrasound images requires medical expertise and may be time-consuming. Therefore, artificial intelligence and deep learning techniques can assist clinicians by providing automated medical image analysis.

Convolutional Neural Networks (CNNs) are among the most successful deep learning approaches for image classification tasks because they automatically learn spatial features directly from image data.

---

## 3.2 Problem Statement

Manual PCOS ultrasound analysis may be affected by:

* human interpretation variability
* diagnostic delays
* large image volumes
* requirement for expert radiologists

This project aims to build a CNN-based system capable of automatically classifying ultrasound images into:

* infected (PCOS)
* noninfected (normal)

---

## 3.3 Objectives

The objectives of this project are:

1. Understand and preprocess the PCOS ultrasound dataset.
2. Build a CNN model for binary image classification.
3. Handle dataset imbalance using appropriate techniques.
4. Apply data augmentation to improve generalization.
5. Evaluate the CNN using multiple medical classification metrics.
6. Analyze overfitting and threshold behavior.
7. Develop a simple Streamlit prediction interface.

