# 5. Data Preprocessing

## 5.1 Data Cleaning

The preprocessing stage included:

* checking corrupted images
* removing invalid files
* validating image paths
* ensuring correct labels

---

## 5.2 Image Resizing

All images were resized to:

224 × 224 × 3

This standardized the image dimensions for CNN training.

---

## 5.3 Normalization

Pixel values were normalized to the range:

[0, 1]

using:

x = x / 255

Normalization improves CNN training stability and convergence.

---

## 5.4 Train/Validation/Test Split

The dataset was divided into:

| Dataset    | Percentage |
| ---------- | ---------- |
| Training   | 70%        |
| Validation | 15%        |
| Testing    | 15%        |

The test set remained untouched until the final evaluation stage.

---

## 5.5 Data Augmentation

To improve generalization and reduce overfitting, data augmentation was applied only to the training set.

The augmentation techniques included:

* rotation
* width shift
* height shift
* zoom
* horizontal flip

These transformations helped the model learn more robust visual patterns.

---

## 5.6 Imbalance Handling

The dataset was moderately imbalanced.

To address this issue, class weights were calculated and applied during training:

* minority class received higher weight
* majority class received lower weight

This helped reduce bias toward the dominant class.

---

